                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "372981b2-5c66-44e6-bdb9-58c286d4f48f",
                        "source_entry_id": "e0f33615-0f49-31de-9245-bf6117b9b308",
                        "source_sense_id": "28e0a039-876f-3bff-9e82-2d6a0a4299f4",
                        "target_lang_word": "good-natured",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "good-natured",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a15f1e2f-aa47-3188-841e-6b47575744c0",
                                        "entry_id": "f835f60f-2b8f-3627-8ab8-80ce822e9151",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having or showing an amicable, kindly disposition."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "06f6abb7-887e-40fd-bfb1-bddb0bfc37bd",
                                                "sense_id": "a15f1e2f-aa47-3188-841e-6b47575744c0",
                                                "text": "“It is singular,” said the Lady, addressing Warden; “the animal is not only so good-natured to all, but so particularly fond of children.[…]”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3edaae72-8253-4c6d-8790-19a996cb45f1",
                                                "sense_id": "a15f1e2f-aa47-3188-841e-6b47575744c0",
                                                "text": "For the people who were shovelling away on the house-tops were jovial and full of glee; calling out to one another from the parapets, and now and then exchanging a facetious snowball—better-natured missile far than many a wordy jest—laughing heartily if it went right, and not less heartily if it went wrong."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c068a455-d0aa-400d-95bb-3003f50c4026",
                                                "sense_id": "a15f1e2f-aa47-3188-841e-6b47575744c0",
                                                "text": "There are a good many of these girls whom it is quite enough to spoil the temper of the best-natured woman in the world to have in the house with them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "94e05742-ccc2-4708-b3c5-31633280544f",
                                                "sense_id": "a15f1e2f-aa47-3188-841e-6b47575744c0",
                                                "text": "Rasmus was a tall, powerful man, with a weather-beaten, furrowed face of a good-natured expression."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a55032ff-beb2-4eaa-9343-387b886ce1b8",
                                                "sense_id": "a15f1e2f-aa47-3188-841e-6b47575744c0",
                                                "text": "However, the immediate howls of outrage from the industry were in many cases less than good-natured."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "359ed1ae-de8a-4614-8e73-31b85f9edfd9",
                                                "sense_id": "a15f1e2f-aa47-3188-841e-6b47575744c0",
                                                "text": "I had a rival for Marcel’s affections, a boy who later became the king of recorded classical music and confrère of Herbert von Karajan. I was vile to this poor chap who, like a cheerful Papageno, was much better-natured than I was."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f4805254-80a2-4604-957b-6b62fd9a5e63",
                        "source_entry_id": "e0f33615-0f49-31de-9245-bf6117b9b308",
                        "source_sense_id": "28e0a039-876f-3bff-9e82-2d6a0a4299f4",
